{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>And you I will scatter among the nations.</b> This is a harsh measure — for when the people of a province are exiled to one place, they see one another and take comfort; but Israel is scattered like winnowing — like a man winnowing barley with a sieve, and not one of them clings to its fellow (ibid.)." "<b>And I will draw [the sword].</b> As when a sword is drawn, the sheath is emptied; and its midrash: a sword unsheathed after you does not return quickly, like a man who pours out water and it does not return (Sifra)." "<b>And your land shall be a desolation.</b> That you shall not hasten to return into it, and consequently your cities will be desolate — appearing to you as destroyed; for when a man is exiled from his house and his vineyard and his city and will ultimately return, it is as though his vineyard and his house are not destroyed. Thus it is taught in Tosefta Kippurim."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:47.707712172Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}